   Remote registry read failure blocks managed startup. A CLI daemon is reused
   only after its password policy fits; foreground servers are never stopped.
   Keep server running controls stopping the managed CLI daemon on disconnect.
+  Selecting another host preserves the previous SSH connection for background
+  work; selection alone does not require a remote stop. Remote stop is best
+  effort, including for an adopted managed daemon with disconnect authority.
   An interrupted forward makes at most 5 key/agent reconnect attempts with
   backoff. A new password or trust decision requires explicit Retry.
   Its cleanup executor outlives the API connection. App quit drains accepted
   writes first, then stops every retained SSH session and awaits its bounded
   remote-stop receipt before releasing client runtimes.
+  `ssh_cleanup.rs` defines private cleanup observations. Receipt completion means
+  the worker ended, independently of remote success. Stop JSON distinguishes a
+  confirmed stop, explicit failure, authoritative absence and uncertainty. The
+  existing CLI serve JSON supplies the launched daemon's port and PID; missing
+  acknowledgements grant no destructive port-based reconciliation. Adopted
+  daemons capture their existing CLI status identity. Stop rechecks that identity
+  and suppresses the command if it is missing or changed. CLI status and stop are
+  separate operations, so they do not provide an atomic conditional stop or
+  protection against PID reuse. Local reports retain group-signal outcomes and
+  leader-reap observation separately; helper cleanup remains unconfirmed.
+  Reports add no close veto, UI, timeout or host-switch policy. Reliable terminal
+  preflight and stronger process/session custody belong to their own lifecycle
+  owners; the final GPUI shutdown hook remains bounded best-effort cleanup.
